  "verbalization": "Bornyl chloride, (-)- is consistently identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Dendocarbin K and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, all of which share a common target of NH-6. This suggests a hierarchical relationship where Bornyl chloride, (-)- acts as a precursor or modulator that ultimately leads to the activation of NH-6 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence points to a pathway where the chemical structure of Bornyl chloride, (-)- may influence the binding or activity of its targets, which then converge on NH-6. The presence of multiple overlapping targets, including different metabolites and compounds, supports the idea that NH-6 is a downstream effector in this network. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Bornyl chloride, (-)- to play a role in the regulation of NH-6 through a complex, multi-step mechanism.",
